# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ScholarScout environment variables
# EVERYTHING HERE IS OPTIONAL. The core application runs with zero API keys.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Optional: GitHub-backed "full crawl" for the Update Now button ──────────
# When set, the Update Now button ALSO offers dispatching the full GitHub
# Actions ingestion workflow (which commits fresh data to the repository).
# Create a fine-grained personal access token with "Actions: read & write"
# on your ScholarScout repository only.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
# GITHUB_REPO=your-username/scholarscout

# ── Optional: shared secret protecting the serverless update endpoint ───────
# If set, POST /api/update requires the header  x-update-key: <value>.
# Recommended once deployed publicly; leave unset for local development.
# UPDATE_SECRET=

# ── Optional: future AI summarization provider (NOT required) ────────────────
# The matching/summarization layer is rule-based and fully functional without
# this. If you ever plug in a provider, wire it in src/server/enrich.ts.
# AI_PROVIDER=
# AI_API_KEY=
